- `action(n1, "start")`: Hallucinates a preliminary step; the source description explicitly begins with "BUSINESS PROCESS REQUIREMENTS" with no prior starting activity (SMC1).
- `action(n4, "IT Design  Development & Functional Test")`: Label omits the comma present in the source text ("IT Design, Development & Functional Test"), compromising node payload fidelity (SMC2).
- `actor(a_default, "Default", [...])`: Assigns a single "Default" actor to every node (including non-executable `init`, `end`, `branch`, and `converge` elements), despite the source text containing zero information about participants or responsibilities (SMC7).